  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n4 : 33 :: ? : 109 :: 8 : 257\n\n**Logic: Second number = [{(First no.)³ + 2} ÷ 2]**\n\n**4 : 33 →**\n\n⇒ [{(4)³ + 2} ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ [(64 + 2) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (66 ÷ 2) = 33\n\n**8 : 257 →**\n\n⇒ [{(8)3 + 2} ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ [(512 + 2) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (514 ÷ 2) = 257\n\n**Similarly, for '? : 109' →**\n\n⇒ [{(Y)3 + 2} ÷ 2] = 109\n\n⇒ [{(Y)3 + 2}] = (109 × 2)\n\n⇒ (Y)³ = 218 - 2\n\n⇒ (Y)3 = 216\n\n⇒** Y = 6**\n\nHere, **'6 : 109'** is the correct pair.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (3)\".",
